  "_comment": "Gochujang shared skin/rig CATALOG — the studio's reusable player-rig library, shipped WITH the engine (travels via the gochujang git package; a fork git-subtree-pulls and gets every rig). This is an ASSET MANIFEST, not game logic: it lists rigs by a STABLE id, it does not branch on anything (Rule 2 stays clean — engine CODE never names a rig). skinManager default-loads it (SkinManager.DEFAULT_CATALOG) and the GAME subsets it via app.api.skins.enable([...ids]) + prices/policy via setPrices/configure. A rig appearing here does NOT load it — this is ~KB of text; the 3D template/material loads lazily only when a player actually wears it, and only enabled ids are built into skinMap.",
  "_contract": "skinIndex is a FROZEN cross-game id: it is the netcode `animal` uint8 field AND the saved currentSkinId. APPEND-ONLY — never renumber an existing id; new rigs take a new unused id (uint8, so ids 1..255). The numbering is intentionally sparse. funnyChar (6) is the customizable human avatar (has part-slots + a typeName type-list asset, referenced BY NAME so it resolves per-project); every other rig is a fixed-form skin (parts:[], typeName:null). typeName resolves to a json asset whose .resources is the part-type name list (e.g. Hat_038).",
